{"term":"intervene","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:9a1e215494c6296ae4","definition":"To become involved in a situation, so as to alter or prevent an action.","example":"The police had to be called to intervene in the fight.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["interfere","step in"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["intervenability","intervenable","intervenee","intervenor","interventive","reintervene"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intervene#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a551223ece42954a1f","definition":"To occur, fall, or come between, points of time, or events.","example":"An instant intervened between the flash and the report.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["elapse"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["intervenability","intervenable","intervenee","intervenor","interventive","reintervene"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intervene#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:06e722642716cc1f28","definition":"To occur or act as an obstacle or delay.","example":"Nothing intervened to prevent the undertaking.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["intervenability","intervenable","intervenee","intervenor","interventive","reintervene"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intervene#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c59e758497e12d31d9","definition":"To say (something) in the middle of a conversation or discussion between other people, or to respond to a situation involving other people.","example":"Young Scarfe stared, astounded. “You haven’t met before,” Mrs. Gould intervened. “Mr. Decoud—Mr. Scarfe.”","pos":"verb","synonyms":["interrupt"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":["intervenability","intervenable","intervenee","intervenor","interventive","reintervene"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intervene#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a686f3157deee9c486","definition":"To come between, or to be between, persons or things.","example":"The Mediterranean intervenes between Europe and Africa.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":["intervenability","intervenable","intervenee","intervenor","interventive","reintervene"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intervene#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:405ec158c066785fc2","definition":"In a suit to which one has not been made a party, to put forward a defense of one's interest in the subject matter.","example":"an application for leave (i.e. permission) to intervene","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["intervenability","intervenable","intervenee","intervenor","interventive","reintervene"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intervene#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈviːn/"},"wordFamily":["intervenability","intervenable","intervenee","intervenor","interventive","reintervene"]}